WHAT THIS COVERS
The curated data tables, the schema and data dictionary, the documentation and
the build/QC code in this directory (toxicity/hydrocephalus/) are released under
the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License. You are free to
share and adapt this material for any purpose, including commercially, provided
you give appropriate credit.

Full licence text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

WHAT THIS DOES NOT COVER
This grant applies to the curation — the tables, the structure, the
documentation and the code. It does NOT relicense the underlying third-party
sources, which are never redistributed here in full. Each measurement row
records its own rights status in the `redistribution` column:

  public_domain        US Government works (ClinicalTrials.gov, FAERS, DailyMed
                       prescribing information, eCFR). Values may be reproduced.
  cc_by                Open-access articles under CC BY. Values may be
                       reproduced with attribution to the original article.
  cc_by_nc             Open-access articles under a non-commercial licence.
  summary_stat_only    Sources whose licence carries a no-derivatives term; only
                       abstract-level summary statistics are carried, and no
                       underlying table or figure is reproduced.
  verify               Rights of reuse were NOT established for this source in
                       the curation session. The verbatim text is quoted as
                       evidence; a redistributor should resolve the licence
                       before republishing those values.

Anyone redistributing derived values should check that column, not this file.

CITATION
Cite this dataset AND the underlying primary sources listed in
data/sources.csv. Every row carries source_id, source_ref and an exact
source_location so any value can be traced and attributed.

NO WARRANTY
This dataset is a curation of published data, provided as-is and without
warranty of any kind. All severity grades ship as `grade_status = provisional`
and have not been reviewed by a subject-matter expert. It is a research
resource. It is not medical advice, and it must not be used to make decisions
about the care of any patient.
